2b:Tbcc,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://www.raulji.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Gujarat","item":"https://www.raulji.com/gujarat/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Ahmedabad","item":"https://www.raulji.com/ahmedabad/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"LLP","item":"https://www.raulji.com/ahmedabad/llp-registration/"}]},{"@type":"Service","@id":"https://www.raulji.com/ahmedabad/llp-registration/#service","name":"LLP Registration in Ahmedabad","description":"The LLP does its best work in Ahmedabad among two groups. The first is the city's professional services cluster: chartered accountants, architects, designers, agencies and consultancies around Prahlad Nagar, Bodakdev and Navrangpura, where the business is partner-run, will never issue equity, and mainly wants personal assets kept clear of business claims.","url":"https://www.raulji.com/ahmedabad/llp-registration/","serviceType":"LLP Registration","provider":{"@id":"https://www.raulji.com/#organization"},"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Ahmedabad","containedInPlace":{"@type":"AdministrativeArea","name":"Ahmedabad district, Gujarat"}},"offers":{"@type":"Offer","priceCurrency":"INR","price":"7999","description":"One-time professional fee. Government filing fees and the stamp duty on the LLP Agreement are charged separately and vary by state and contribution.","url":"https://www.raulji.com/ahmedabad/llp-registration/"}},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Should my Ahmedabad partnership firm convert to an LLP?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on what is worrying you. If it is personal liability for business debts, then yes, an LLP addresses exactly that while keeping the partner structure you already have. If the firm is small, trades on its own funds and has no liability exposure that concerns you, the conversion may not be worth the disruption to PAN, bank mandates and GST registration."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is an LLP enough for a large Ahmedabad corporate customer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually yes. An LLP is a body corporate on the MCA register with a registration number that a procurement team can verify, which is what most vendor onboarding checks are actually looking for. A few tender and procurement processes specify a company, so if you are registering for one particular buyer, read their eligibility clause before you choose."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much less compliance is an LLP than a company?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Materially less. An LLP files two annual forms and only needs audit once turnover exceeds Rs 40 lakh or contribution exceeds Rs 25 lakh. A Private Limited Company needs statutory audit from its first year regardless of turnover, plus its own annual filings, board meetings and minutes. Over several years that difference is substantial."}}]}]}21:[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2b"}}],["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Breadcrumb","className":"container-wide pt-28 md:pt-32","children":["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":["$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f"]}]}],"$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34","$L35","$L36","$L37"]
